<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ cover_site_domain }}</title>
  <style>
    body { max-width: 40rem; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; font: 17px/1.6 Georgia, serif; color: #222; background: #fdfdfb; }
    header { border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0; }
    time { color: #888; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    footer { border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin-top: 3rem; color: #888; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>{{ cover_site_domain }}</h1>
    <p>Notes on film photography, slow mornings and things I fix around the house.</p>
  </header>

  <article>
    <h2>Developing at home, second attempt</h2>
    <time datetime="2026-09-14">September 14, 2026</time>
    <p>Kept the developer at 20 °C this time and the negatives came out much less dense. Agitation every minute instead of every thirty seconds made the skies smoother too.</p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h2>A cheap scanning setup</h2>
    <time datetime="2026-07-02">July 2, 2026</time>
    <p>An old macro lens, a light pad and a piece of cardboard with a slot cut for the film strip. Not perfect, but good enough for sharing contact sheets with friends.</p>
  </article>

  <article>
    <h2>Fixing the balcony door</h2>
    <time datetime="2026-04-19">April 19, 2026</time>
    <p>The hinge had dropped a few millimetres. Two turns on the adjustment screw and the draft is gone. Writing it down so I remember which screw next winter.</p>
  </article>

  <footer>
    <p>Written slowly, updated rarely.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
